#Here's the git documentation page on .gitignore files.  See how they work, where they can be located, and how patterns within them function:
#https://git-scm.com/docs/gitignore

#See GitHub's repo with all the templates that are used to populate the menu when you create a .gitignore using the GitHub ui:
#https://github.com/github/gitignore

#The following is a basic list of files and directories that could be commonly ignored, but it may be necessary to build a more context sensitive .gitignore for any given repo.
#In order to activate any of these patterns, you will need to remove the # comment marker.

#Global
#*.png
#*.jpg
#*.jpeg
#*.svg
#*.pdf
#*.csv
#*.xlsx
#*.xls

#Java
# Compiled class file
#*.class
# Package Files #
#*.jar
#*.war
#*.ear
#*.zip
#*.tar.gz
#*.rar

#Javascript
#node_modules/
#public/
#.config
#.prettier
#.env

#Python
#*.pyc

#MacOS
#.DS_Store
#.Trashes

#Environment vars and venv
.env
.venv/